    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0595" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg495"/>

                <head>No. 323.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Edward
                            Thornton to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-11-14"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 14,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose copy of a
                    letter addressed to the Marquis of Salisbury by Mr. George Kelly, of Mazatlan,
                    Mexico, together <pb facs="0596" n="496" xml:id="pg496"/> with a copy of the
                    Mexican custom-house regulations to which that letter refers, and under the
                    provisions of which it would appear that the captain of the American steamer
                    Newbern was imprisoned in September last.</p>
                <p>Lord Salisbury has instructed me to inquire whether the United States Government
                    is aware of the existence of these regulations, and whether it proposes to take
                    any steps to procure their modification or removal.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ED W’D THORNTON.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d323-a1.xml" xpointer="d323-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d323-a2.xml" xpointer="d323-a2"/>
